  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::170850",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is likely to interact with Kcng3 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine binds to Kcna6, Kcnf1, or Kcnv2, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is then associated with Kcng3, indicating a potential functional link between these molecules. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Dalfampridine potentially modulating the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels, which in turn may influence Kcng3. The overlapping roles of these potassium channels in cellular function imply that Dalfampridine could exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by altering channel activity or function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Dalfampridine in regulating potassium channel activity, which may have implications for cellular electrophysiology and related physiological processes.",
